# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/s7 window (the ship-7 candidate; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/s7 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt and
# ORDER-SHIP.txt have the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules of the two runs.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW AND THE SHIP: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-s7-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft and the ship-7 profile baked as the serving default
# (sed -i 's/tp4-s7-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# C2_MODEL_REPO / C2_MODEL_REVISION (qwen_c2_checkpoint.py): a job that carries them serves the Swift checkpoint (what production serves) from its own converted-weight directory; the keys are the same in every
# smoke and prefix job of this pack, so each pair differs by the profile alone. The replay and build steps do not forward the selection (the job reader refuses the keys beside them): they run the base checkpoint.
# T2B (TIMED, the CANDIDATE of the T2 pair): the ship-7 candidate, a TRAFFIC profile under the owner waiver the ship-7 decision records (a PENDING one boots in a smoke and
# logs the word) c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s7 on Swift. Tests: concurrent8_steady (the octo rounds, required by the smoke check) and
# agent_turns8 (EIGHT sessions of the agent_turns plan, every seat busy). OPTIONAL: it runs when the window has the minutes. agent_turns (6 sessions of 64k, 128k and 200k
# tokens, 12 returning turns each) is the MAIN JUDGE: the ship-5 window's T1B number (50.36 tok/s aggregate, returning turn first token p50 1.46 s, p90 2.33 s) is its
# baseline. agent_turns8 is EIGHT sessions weighted like production traffic (contexts of 24k to 80k tokens and one of ~200k, about 550k tokens in all, mean ~69k against
# production's ~59k; answers capped at 300 to 1,080 tokens, mean 690 like production's; the same gaps and 12 turns), every seat busy, no new turn after 25 minutes, an
# estimate of 15 minutes: the production load, where WC (2 or 4 users) and the governor (1 or 2 decoders) mostly sit out, so the pair says whether anything is LOST there.
# Compare it with its own control leg, never with agent_turns. Read both legs with `python3 scripts/ci/agent_turns.py report --smoke-log <smoke> --container-log <container>
# --test <name>`: the rates, the TTFT by context bucket, the tokens re-prefilled, the per-live table; the per-turn answer hashes must be EQUAL between the legs. Every boot
# a fresh reset. READ: c2_smoke_check clean on both legs; python3 scripts/ci/agent_turns.py report --test agent_turns8 on each leg side by side; the answer hashes equal; no
# LOSS of the candidate against the control outside the boot-to-boot drift. NO-GO for the candidate: any text difference against the control, an audit mismatch, a latch or
# fall-back line of any of the five groups, a fall-back line beyond the octo block's one WC line, a floor violation (a decode gap over 8 s), an allocator or admission
# failure, an eight-live window outside the boot-to-boot drift of the control, a loss in the restore pair, an errored or timed-out agent request. A failing lever is taken
# out by deleting its line from the ship entry of scripts/ci/fusion-wp/S7.json (and, for seed first and the ledger trim, from the waiver's levers) and regenerating (a new
# build): QWEN_PREFIX_TIER_IO_THREADS with QWEN_PREFIX_TIER_VERIFY_THREADS, QWEN_FAST_ADMISSION_SEED_FIRST, QWEN_FAST_ADMISSION_LEDGER_TRIM, QWEN_FAST_LOOKUP_DRAFT,
# QWEN_FAST_PREFILL_TAIL_TRACE. RUN WITH THE CI PAUSED: the ARC runner sets are at ZERO for this job (ORDER, ARC-ZERO); no build, no CI push, no other job beside it.
# CHECKPOINT READ (the workflow passes c2_smoke_check.py --expect-checkpoint): the container log holds "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint
# ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b@b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4 key=... weight_cache=.../weights-ckpt/<key> base_cache=... (the base cache is not read or written)"
# once, a "weight cache ...: found" line (the cache the Swift window built; this pack never builds it) and the worker's "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint bound ..." line; the models
# answer names ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b. TELEMETRY (C2_TELEMETRY=1, scripts/ci/card_telemetry.py): the read-only ARC sidecar samples every chip once a second through
# the smoke step; the first [TELEMETRY] line must say decode check ok. A rate difference that comes with a different loaded AICLK between the arms is the clocks, not the
# lever. Duration (estimate): 15 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-s7-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s7
C2_MODEL_REPO=ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b
C2_MODEL_REVISION=b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,concurrent8_steady,agent_turns8
C2_TELEMETRY=1
C2_BOX_MINUTES=40
